    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d636">

                <pb facs="0722" n="710" sameAs="frus:frus1943v02/pg710"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">811.79652/27: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Spain</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Hayes</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Madrid</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1943-11-18T00:00:00+01:00">November 18,
                            1943—midnight</date>.<lb/>[Received November 19—5:45 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>3405. Jordana told me this morning that the Council of Ministers has approved our
                    request for landing rights for American commercial airlines. Spanish Government
                    proposes to create a special commission with full powers to agree to details,
                    such as particular airports to be used, number and types of planes, et cetera.
                    He would be glad if I named a representative or representatives of the Embassy
                    to meet with this commission, and he was anxious that details be arranged as
                    quickly as possible. I said I would do so.</p>
                <p>I suggest Department inform me as promptly as possible details requested in my
                    3094, October 23, 6 p.m.,<anchor n="65" xml:id="d636-f1"/> as well as any other
                    details it can. I also suggest that Colonel Cousland, recently appointed
                    Assistant Military Air Attaché familiarize himself with American end of this
                    subject before he leaves United States.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Hayes</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
